Title:
PhantomCtx — Activation Context Hijacking Evasion Tool

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- PhantomCtx automates Windows Activation Context (SxS manifest) hijacking to force signed executables to load an attacker-controlled DLL without requiring a “vulnerable” binary.  
- It targets the loader’s DLL resolution step for SxS manifest redirection by modifying the Activation Context’s DLL redirection table used via `PEB.ActivationContextData`.  
- The key contribution is an EDR-evasion-oriented implementation that avoids common remote memory write/injection telemetry by unmapping the original Activation Context section view and remapping a malicious, read-only section at the same address (using `NtUnmapViewOfSection` + section mapping), eliminating the need to overwrite the PEB pointer.  
- It supports recon of Activation Context blobs, hijacking during process spawn (recommended) or against already-running processes, and can “steal” a valid Activation Context from another process (e.g., `explorer.exe`) when the target lacks a DLL redirection section.  
- Useful primarily for red teams and offensive security researchers focusing on stealthy DLL loading, signed-binary execution, and loader/EDR tradecraft.

Technical Focus:
- Windows Activation Contexts (SxS) and DLL redirection tables
- Windows loader DLL resolution order (IAT vs `LoadLibrary`)
- PEB internals (`PEB.ActivationContextData`) and process memory layout
- Section view unmapping/remapping for in-place structure replacement
- NT syscalls/APIs: `NtUnmapViewOfSection`, `NtReadVirtualMemory`, process creation/resume
- DLL proxying/export forwarding to preserve target stability

Use Cases:
- Covert DLL loading into signed Microsoft/third-party executables for OPSEC
- Bypassing EDR detections tied to `WriteProcessMemory`/`NtWriteVirtualMemory`-style injection
- Redirection-based “sideloading” when no classic DLL search-order weakness exists
- Runtime hijacking experiments where a process later loads a target DLL by name
- Building/patching Activation Context redirection entries for specific imported DLLs

Keywords:
Activation Context, SxS manifest, DLL redirection, PEB.ActivationContextData, Windows loader, IAT, LoadLibrary, NtUnmapViewOfSection, section mapping, NtReadVirtualMemory, CreateProcessW, suspended process, EDR evasion, DLL proxying, export forwarding, signed binary abuse, process injection alternative, mpnotify.exe, explorer.exe, Elastic EDR/XDR